# Shared AI Guidance

Canonical AI guidance lives in `.ai/`. See `.ai/README.md` and root `AGENTS.md`. Prefer adding durable agent instructions there, with `.cursor/` and `.claude/` containing lightweight references.

**Architecture invariants (enforced by ESLint in `apps/`):** Dashboard and www must not import `@workspace/database`, `@workspace/database/client`, or `@prisma/client` — use domain packages and repos. All apps under `apps/` must not import `lucide-react` — use `@workspace/ui/components/icon-for`.

When adding or changing database models, Prisma schema, model repositories, or CRUD data access, read `.ai/skills/add-data-model-to-database/SKILL.md` before making changes.

When adding new pages, routes, or feature page content to any Next.js app, read `.ai/skills/add-new-page/SKILL.md` before making changes.

When adding a new app to the monorepo, creating a new directory or package.json under `apps/`, or setting up any new runnable service (Next.js app, API server, webhook listener, worker, preview server, etc.), read `.ai/skills/add-new-app/SKILL.md` before making changes.

When adding or using icons in app code (apps/*), read `.ai/skills/add-icon/SKILL.md` before making changes. Never import directly from lucide-react in app code.

When displaying dates or timestamps in any UI component (apps/* or packages/ui), use `formatDate()` from `@workspace/common`. Read `.ai/conventions/format-date.md` before writing date display code.

When creating a new project-level AI skill (SKILL.md), read `.ai/skills/create-skill/SKILL.md` before making changes.

When the user wants to stress-test a plan, get grilled on their design, mentions "grill me", or invokes `/grill-me-matt`, read `.ai/skills/grill-me-matt/SKILL.md` before proceeding.

When adding a modal, dialog, confirm dialog, alert dialog, drawer, or any overlay triggered by a user action, read `.ai/skills/add-modal-or-confirm-dialog/SKILL.md` before making changes.

When adding a paginated list/table, bulk row selection, bulk export, or "add selected to …" flows to a dashboard list, read `.ai/skills/create-data-table/SKILL.md` before making changes.

When adding or editing LLM instruction files (rules, skills, conventions), read `.ai/conventions/ai-guidance-files.md` before making changes.

When creating or updating implementation plans (`docs/superpowers/plans/`) or design specs (`docs/superpowers/specs/`), read `.ai/conventions/critical-tests-in-plans.md` first. Copy from `docs/superpowers/plans/_template.md` or `docs/superpowers/specs/_template.md` when starting a new doc. Every plan and spec **must** include a `## Critical Tests` section (high-value unit tests, colocated paths) before task breakdown — a doc without it is incomplete.

When adding or moving unit tests, read `.ai/conventions/colocated-tests.md` before making changes.

When finishing a development branch with a completed plan, read `.ai/conventions/plan-archival.md` before making changes.

Always use ESM `import`/`export` syntax. Never use `require()` or `module.exports`. This applies to all source code, config files, scripts, and generated code across the entire monorepo.
